.TH MFCJ5720DW_INK 1 "November 2026" "MFC-J5720DW driver" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mfcj5720dw_ink \- report Brother ink estimates to CUPS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mfcj5720dw_ink
.B \-\-report-levels
.br
.B mfcj5720dw_ink
.I job-id user title copies options
.RI [ file ]
.br
.B mfcj5720dw_ink
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
This native CUPS filter queries the MFC-J5720DW maintenance OID through
the CUPS side channel on file descriptor 4. The network backend performs
the read-only SNMP GET using its configured community.
No SNMP SET, printer command or document data is sent by this filter.
.PP
The four ink estimates are reported to the scheduler as marker attributes
on stderr, in black, cyan, magenta, yellow order. Values are rounded to whole
percentages; a nonzero estimate smaller than one percent is shown as one.
Low-ink status is reported at five percent or less, empty only at exactly zero.
These values are printer estimates, not measured ink volumes.
The supply type is ink, recognized by CUPS clients including GNOME 50.
.PP
The raster filter calls the shared reporting function before rendering each job.
Updates can also be requested without printing through a CUPS command job.
The PPD advertises only ReportLevels and disables generic SNMP supply polling
because this printer's standard Printer-MIB does not return usable percentages.
.SH COMMAND FILE
With the CUPS positional arguments, read the named file or stdin.
The first line must be #CUPS-COMMAND. Only ReportLevels is supported;
command names are case insensitive. Blank lines and comments are accepted.
The entire file is validated before issuing one query.
.PP
Example, submitting a status request to an existing queue:
.nf
printf '#CUPS-COMMAND\enReportLevels\en' | \e
  lp -d PRINTER -t 'Ink levels' -o document-format=application/vnd.cups-command
.fi
.SH AVAILABILITY
The CUPS network backend must support side-channel SNMP queries.
LPD is validated for this model. USB and backends without this capability
cannot provide levels through this filter.
Without a valid reply, no marker values are emitted: CUPS retains its last
successful reading. The raster filter ignores query failures.
.PP
The query timeout is three seconds for each side-channel read or write.
There is no background polling while the queue is idle; use ReportLevels
after changing a cartridge to refresh without printing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means success or help. One means a failed query, invalid response or
invalid command file. Two indicates an invalid invocation.
Normal reporting never writes to stdout.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/lib/cups/filter/mfcj5720dw_ink
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rastertomfcj5720dw (1),
.BR lp (1)
